Description: segment: stage-rename HLS chunks (scaleplex)
 ffmpeg's ssegment muxer writes chunks directly to their canonical
 filename and POSTs the segment_list CSV row to the URL handler as
 soon as the segment closes. When PMS reads the chunk over the same
 NFS mount the worker writes to (scaleplex's setup), it can open
 the file mid-write and serve a 0-byte or partial response. Plex
 clients treat the empty segment as a gap and jump forward,
 surfacing as "video forwarded multiple seconds" skips.
 .
 This patch mirrors Plex Transcoder's libavformat/segment.c stage-
 rename pattern. Each chunk is written to <final>.tmp; immediately
 after av_write_trailer (and BEFORE the segment_list CSV row is
 POSTed) the .tmp file is rename()'d to the final canonical name.
 PMS only ever opens the canonical filename, and only after the
 atomic rename — so it always sees a complete chunk. Plex's
 version gates on `!seg->list`; ours always fires because our
 seg->list is the URL handler that informs PMS, so the race
 between row POST and PMS open is exactly what stage-rename
 closes.
 .
 No new option; no opt-in. The added work per chunk is one
 rename() syscall (microseconds). avio_close has already flushed
 ffmpeg's userspace buffer to the kernel before this rename, so
 the file's contents are complete; rename atomicity guarantees
 PMS never observes a partial canonical name.
 .
 Earlier iteration of this patch added an `-segment_fsync` option
 to force an NFS COMMIT before the rename. Live testing on Big
 Hero 6 4K HDR HEVC + PGS overlay confirmed rename-only is the
 actual fix — kernel page-cache coherence between writer (worker
 pod) and reader (PMS pod) on the same NFS mount makes the
 server-side commit irrelevant for the consistency we need.
 Stage-rename eliminates the skip; fsync was over-engineering at
 a ~20% encoder pace cost.
Origin: backport (minimal), https://github.com/Diagonactic/plex-new-transcoder
        plex-ffmpeg-source/NewPlexTranscoder/libavformat/segment.c
        (stage-rename pattern; Plex gates on !seg->list, ours always fires)
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-12
---
--- a/libavformat/segment.c	2026-05-12 19:26:10.459932320 +0200
+++ b/libavformat/segment.c	2026-05-12 20:28:26.487799177 +0200
@@ -231,6 +231,27 @@
              seg->entry_prefix ? seg->entry_prefix : "",
              av_basename(oc->url));
 
+    /* scaleplex: stage-rename. Write chunk to <final>.tmp; rename to
+     * final in segment_end before the segment_list CSV row gets
+     * POSTed. The CSV row (cur_entry.filename above) stays as the
+     * FINAL name so PMS receives the canonical filename and only
+     * ever opens it after the atomic rename — never mid-write.
+     * Without this, ffmpeg writes directly to the canonical filename
+     * which PMS may open mid-write via the shared NFS mount and
+     * serve as 0 bytes / partial → Plex client treats the segment
+     * as a gap and jumps forward. Mirrors Plex Transcoder's pattern
+     * in libavformat/segment.c (their version is gated on
+     * `!seg->list`; we always need it because seg->list is the URL
+     * handler that informs PMS). */
+    {
+        size_t tmp_size = strlen(oc->url) + 5; /* + ".tmp\0" */
+        char *tmp_url = av_malloc(tmp_size);
+        if (!tmp_url)
+            return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
+        snprintf(tmp_url, tmp_size, "%s.tmp", oc->url);
+        ff_format_set_url(oc, tmp_url);
+    }
+
     return 0;
 }
 
@@ -372,6 +393,24 @@
         av_log(s, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Failure occurred when ending segment '%s'\n",
                oc->url);
 
+    /* scaleplex: stage-rename .tmp → final BEFORE the segment_list
+     * CSV row is POSTed below. See set_segment_filename for the
+     * matching .tmp suffix on chunk open. */
+    if (oc->url) {
+        size_t url_len = strlen(oc->url);
+        if (url_len > 4 && !strcmp(oc->url + url_len - 4, ".tmp")) {
+            char *final_url = av_strdup(oc->url);
+            if (final_url) {
+                final_url[url_len - 4] = '\0';
+                if (rename(oc->url, final_url) < 0)
+                    av_log(s, AV_LOG_WARNING,
+                           "scaleplex: rename('%s' -> '%s') failed: %s\n",
+                           oc->url, final_url, av_err2str(AVERROR(errno)));
+                ff_format_set_url(oc, final_url);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     if (seg->list) {
         if (seg->list_size || seg->list_type == LIST_TYPE_M3U8) {
             SegmentListEntry *entry = av_mallocz(sizeof(*entry));
